451,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1234911-investigation-how-to-do-pro-forma-investigation-when-you-allready-know-the-truth?p=1235586#post1235586\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sometimes you can fabricate it; fake evidence is planted to falsely convict people, there's no reason that fake evidence can't be planted to facilitate legitimate convictions in situations where supernatural methods were used to hide the crime.<br /> <br /> Powers like Auspex or various spells can also simply reveal the location of mundane evidence. Auspex's <i>Lay Open the Mind</i>, for example, would allow you to simply go through the memories of the person step by step to see where they might have left evidence.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yeah. Honestly that may be easier sometimes. Or you could just used Dominate (vampire) or Mind(Mage) to make the bad guy confess. Mages could do any sort of devious things that Im not sure they are worth being included here. When the splat has an entire section based of coming up with new uses for their powers then someone is going to think up something clever to make it work.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13691-margul","name":"Margul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}